# ProVerif installation transcript (all commands run as root on Ubuntu 24.04, 2026-11-04)
# Route: apt (opam, ocaml) -> opam init (system compiler) -> opam install proverif.
# opam fetched every source archive from its cache mirror https://opam.ocaml.org/cache and verified it against
# the checksum in the opam package file; no binary or source was fetched by any other route.
# The first 'opam install' stopped because the depext libgtk2.0-dev (needed by lablgtk, a dependency of the
# proverif opam package) was missing; it was installed with apt and 'opam install' was re-run.
# Note: the proxy status page listed an earlier rejected CONNECT to bproverif.inria.fr:443 (502, policy/upstream),
# made before this work started; the INRIA host was not needed because opam's cache mirror served the archive.

